{"_v":1,"id":"dear-england-new-wimbledon-theatre-west-end-2026","cat":"west-end","cs":83,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":6,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Dominic Cavendish","o":"The Telegraph","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/dear-england-olivier-review-joseph-fiennes-gareth-southgate/"},{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/dear-england-national-theatre-review-james-graham-gareth-southgate-harry-kane-b1089139.html","q":"This is a thrilling piece of work, popular and political as Graham always intends his plays to be, and – appropriately – a consummate team effort."},{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/dear-england-review-pitch-perfect-gareth-southgate-brings-the-game-home-f9vf7cgtm"},{"cn":"Sarah Crompton","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/dear-england-at-the-national-theatre-review-the-beautiful-game-in-a-beautiful-play_1404772/","q":"In his hands, aided and abetted by the vigorous direction by Rupert Goold, this story of Gareth Southgate’s vision for the England men’s football team is an absolute blast, a riot of exuberant theatre that is as exciting as Marcus Rashford scoring a hat-trick."},{"cn":"Alistair Smith","o":"The Stage","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/long-reviews/dear-england-review-olivier-theatre-national-theatre-london-joseph-fiennes-james-graham-rupert-goold-gareth-southgate"},{"cn":"Jessie Thomspon","o":"The Independent","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/dear-england-review-national-theatre-b2361490.html","q":"Dear England is ambitious, but often overloaded by the sheer number of events since 2016."},{"cn":"Maryam Philpott","o":"The Reviews Hub","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.thereviewshub.com/dear-engl